From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/19] wasi: take the working directory and home from the environment
 environment

wasi-libc's current_dir() is "/" at start, wherever the process runs;
relative paths reach the real working directory through the kernel's `.`
preopen. main() changes into it: PWD when it is the same directory as `.`
(device and inode, as POSIX shells check PWD), otherwise the path found by
walking `..` up to the root (getcwd(3)'s way). A parent can set a child's
directory without rewriting PWD (Node's spawn with `cwd`): 1.46.0-1 took
that stale PWD and looked for fnox.toml from the parent's directory.

HOME_DIR comes from HOME on WASI.

